-- An NPO body corporate (V-18): before paragraph (ba) was inserted on 16 October 2025 it is within none of Article 2(1)(c) to (h) and is no entity; from that day it is within paragraph (ba).
-- The kinds are those G1 derives from the facts and the vintage; here the vintage of G7 supplies the one fact that changes (whether paragraph (ba) is in force on the day).

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH AN Entity
`an NPO body corporate established under Jersey law, on` day MEANS
    Entity WITH name IS "An NPO body corporate established under Jersey law"
              , `standing on the register` IS `not on the register`
              , `kinds of entity` IS (IF `Endnotes: Article 2(1)(ba) is in force on` day `fav` THEN LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey` ELSE EMPTY)
              , `is a Jersey entity` IS FALSE
              , governors IS EMPTY
              , purposes IS EMPTY

-- V-18: on 15 October 2025 the body is no entity, so 21(5) (a foreign body calling itself a “charity” in connection with its Jersey activities, scenario 17) does not reach it; on 16 October 2025 it is within paragraph (ba) and is an entity.
#ASSERT NOT `the body is an entity within Article 2(1)` (`an NPO body corporate established under Jersey law, on` (YMD 2025 10 15))
#ASSERT `the body is an entity within Article 2(1)` (`an NPO body corporate established under Jersey law, on` (YMD 2025 10 16))
