#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 23 the penalty for the contravention` `paragraph (4) of Article 21`
-- The data: a fine of level 3 carries no imprisonment and the level, and no amount (the amount of level 3 is in the Criminal Justice (Standard Scale of Fines) (Jersey) Law, which is not among the sources);
-- the knowing offences carry 24 months and “a fine” with no maximum stated.
#ASSERT `the penalty of a fine of level 3 on the standard scale`'s `imprisonment up to, in months` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the penalty of a fine of level 3 on the standard scale`'s fine EQUALS `a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3
#ASSERT `the penalty of imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine`'s `imprisonment up to, in months` EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT `the penalty of imprisonment for a term of 2 years and a fine`'s fine EQUALS `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`

-- IP35: the record built with a unit of a term of imprisonment and every other fork as taken.
#ASSERT `the favoured interpretation with the unit of a term of imprisonment` `calendar months` EQUALS `fav`
#ASSERT `the favoured interpretation with the unit of a term of imprisonment` `days` EQUALS `other F7.8`
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) the day on which a term of imprisonment of 2 years beginning on a day ends` (YMD 2027 3 1) (`the favoured interpretation with the unit of a term of imprisonment` `days`) EQUALS YMD 2029 2 28

§§ `The length of the term (F7.8): “imprisonment for a term of 2 years”`

-- Calendar months (reading taken): 2 years from 2027-03-01 ends on 2029-03-01, which is 731 days later because 2028 has a 29 February.
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) the day on which a term of imprisonment of 2 years beginning on a day ends` (YMD 2027 3 1) `fav` EQUALS YMD 2029 3 1
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2027 3 1) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 732 (YMD 2027 3 1) `fav`
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 730 (YMD 2027 3 1) `fav`
-- From 2028-03-01 the two years contain no 29 February (2028-02-29 is before it): 730 days.
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) the day on which a term of imprisonment of 2 years beginning on a day ends` (YMD 2028 3 1) `fav` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 1
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 730 (YMD 2028 3 1) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2028 3 1) `fav`
-- From a 29 February the second anniversary is clamped to 28 February (`add months`): 2028-02-29 to 2030-02-28 is 730 days.
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) the day on which a term of imprisonment of 2 years beginning on a day ends` (YMD 2028 2 29) `fav` EQUALS YMD 2030 2 28
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 730 (YMD 2028 2 29) `fav`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2028 2 29) `fav`
-- The other reading (days): 730 days, wherever the term begins.
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) the day on which a term of imprisonment of 2 years beginning on a day ends` (YMD 2027 3 1) `other F7.8` EQUALS YMD 2029 2 28
#ASSERT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 730 (YMD 2027 3 1) `other F7.8`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 21(9) and 23(7) a sentence of a number of days beginning on a day is within the maximum` 731 (YMD 2027 3 1) `other F7.8`
-- The discriminating case of F7.8: a sentence of 731 days from 2027-03-01 is within two years on one reading and not the other.

§§ `Article 22 — excepted foreign charities`

`UK charity` MEANS `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH
    `established under` IS `the law of the United Kingdom or of a jurisdiction that is part of the United Kingdom`
    `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS TRUE
    `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS TRUE
    `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS FALSE
`prescribed-jurisdiction charity` MEANS `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH
    `established under` IS `the law of a jurisdiction, not Jersey or the United Kingdom or a part of it, that the Minister has prescribed by Order under Article 22(2)(a)(ii)`
    `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS TRUE
    `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS TRUE
    `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS FALSE
`UK body not entitled to call itself a charity` MEANS `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH
    `established under` IS `the law of the United Kingdom or of a jurisdiction that is part of the United Kingdom`
    `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS FALSE
    `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS TRUE
    `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS FALSE
`UK body managed from elsewhere` MEANS `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH
    `established under` IS `the law of the United Kingdom or of a jurisdiction that is part of the United Kingdom`
    `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS TRUE
    `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS FALSE
`body established under Jersey law` MEANS `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH
    `established under` IS `the law of Jersey`
    `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS TRUE
    `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS TRUE
    `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS FALSE
`body established under the law of an unprescribed jurisdiction` MEANS `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH
    `established under` IS `the law of some other jurisdiction`
    `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS TRUE
    `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS TRUE
    `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS FALSE
`specified body that fails the first condition` MEANS `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH
    `established under` IS `the law of some other jurisdiction`
    `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS FALSE
    `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS TRUE
    `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS TRUE
`specified body that is managed from elsewhere` MEANS `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH
    `established under` IS `the law of some other jurisdiction`
    `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS FALSE
    `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS FALSE
    `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `UK charity` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `UK charity` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `prescribed-jurisdiction charity` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `UK body not entitled to call itself a charity` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `UK body managed from elsewhere` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `body established under Jersey law` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `body established under the law of an unprescribed jurisdiction` FALSE
-- Article 22(4): an Order may say that a specified entity is not required to meet the first condition, despite sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) of paragraph (2); the second condition still applies.
#ASSERT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `specified body that fails the first condition` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `specified body that fails the first condition` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` `specified body that is managed from elsewhere` FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 22(2)(a) the entity is established under the law of the United Kingdom or of a prescribed jurisdiction` `UK charity`
#ASSERT `Art 22(2)(a) the entity is established under the law of the United Kingdom or of a prescribed jurisdiction` `prescribed-jurisdiction charity`
