-- The knowing offences, Articles 21(2), 21(4), 21(6) and 23(2): "another person" is the condition that the other person differs from the person making the statement.
--   i: the maker means to mislead only themself: not contravened.   i-entity: the entity means to mislead only itself: not contravened.
--   ii: the maker is the entity itself (Articles 21(7), 23(5)) and the other person a donor: contravened.   iii: a third person and a donor: contravened (the old behaviour).
--   iv: the other person is the entity: contravened; the Law says only "another person", and the code requires only that it differs from the person (an open question for an expert, FRAGMENT-G7 section 7).
--   v: the same name with another identifier is another party: contravened.   vi: a party equal to the maker, constructed again, is the maker: not contravened.
