-- The (b) limbs, Articles 21(1)(b), 21(3)(b), 21(5)(b) and 23(1)(b): "another person" is the condition that the person making the statement is not the entity.
--   b1: the entity caused or permitted a third person to make it: (b) made out, (a) not, the paragraph contravened.
--   b2: the maker is the entity itself: (a) made out, (b) NOT (it is (a)'s case), the paragraph contravened.
--   b3: a third person made it and the entity did not cause or permit it: neither limb.
--   b4: the same name with another identifier is another person: (b) made out.   b5: a party equal to the entity as a party: the entity itself, (a) made out and (b) not.
