-- F7.4 and the penalties with the new parties.  Scenario 06's statement with the entity as the maker and as the other person (the entity means to mislead only itself): the strict offence of Article 21(1) stands,
-- the knowing offence of Article 21(2) is not made out, so one contravention and one penalty (level 3).  With a donor as the other person (Article 21(7)) both are made out.
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` `a Jersey entity` FALSE FALSE TRUE `scenario 06, case i-entity` `fav` EQUALS LIST `paragraph (1) of Article 21`
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23: the penalties for the statement` `a Jersey entity` FALSE FALSE TRUE `scenario 06, case i-entity` `fav` EQUALS LIST `the penalty of a fine of level 3 on the standard scale`
#ASSERT `Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` `a Jersey entity` FALSE FALSE TRUE `scenario 06, case ii` `fav` EQUALS LIST `paragraph (1) of Article 21`, `paragraph (2) of Article 21`
